You're hitting a Postgres syntax error at "exists" in this statement:

alter publication supabase_realtime drop table if exists posts;

Postgres does not support the IF EXISTS clause for ALTER PUBLICATION ... DROP TABLE. That causes the syntax error. I will explain the correct approaches and give safe alternatives you can use.

Details & Fixes
Why the error occurs
The SQL standard/Postgres syntax for ALTER PUBLICATION ... DROP TABLE does not include IF EXISTS. Using IF EXISTS there produces the syntax error you saw.
Correct syntax
To remove a table from a publication, use: ALTER PUBLICATION supabase_realtime DROP TABLE posts;

If you want to drop multiple tables, list them separated by commas: ALTER PUBLICATION supabase_realtime DROP TABLE schema.posts, schema.other_table;

Safe "if exists" behavior Postgres doesn't support IF EXISTS in this statement, so to avoid an error when the table is not part of the publication

To fix the SQL errors and ensure your **Mooderia** metropolis synchronizes perfectly across all devices worldwide, I have refined the database schema to be idempotent (safe to run multiple times) and updated the real-time listeners.

### Corrected SQL Setup
Please run this script in your **Supabase SQL Editor**. It avoids the "already exists" and "syntax error" issues by checking for existing relations before attempting to create or alter them.

```sql
-- 1. Create Tables Safely
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.profiles (
    id uuid REFERENCES auth.users ON DELETE CASCADE PRIMARY KEY,
    username text UNIQUE,
    display_name text,
    email text,
    metadata jsonb DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,
    updated_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.posts (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() PRIMARY KEY,
    author_username text,
    content text,
    likes text[] DEFAULT '{}',
    visibility text DEFAULT 'global',
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.messages (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() PRIMARY KEY,
    sender text,
    recipient text,
    text text,
    is_group boolean DEFAULT false,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now()
);

-- 2. Enable Realtime Safely
-- This block checks if the tables are already in the publication before adding them.
DO $$
BEGIN
    IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_publication_tables WHERE pubname = 'supabase_realtime' AND tablename = 'profiles') THEN
        ALTER PUBLICATION supabase_realtime ADD TABLE public.profiles;
    END IF;

    IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_publication_tables WHERE pubname = 'supabase_realtime' AND tablename = 'posts') THEN
        ALTER PUBLICATION supabase_realtime ADD TABLE public.posts;
    END IF;

    IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_publication_tables WHERE pubname = 'supabase_realtime' AND tablename = 'messages') THEN
        ALTER PUBLICATION supabase_realtime ADD TABLE public.messages;
    END IF;
END $$;

-- 3. Row Level Security (Optional but recommended)
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Public profiles are viewable by everyone." ON public.profiles FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert their own profile." ON public.profiles FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own profile." ON public.profiles FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = id);

ALTER TABLE public.posts ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Posts are viewable by everyone." ON public.posts FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Authenticated users can post." ON public.posts FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.role() = 'authenticated');

ALTER TABLE public.messages ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Messages are viewable by authenticated users." ON public.messages FOR SELECT USING (auth.role() = 'authenticated');
CREATE POLICY "Authenticated users can send messages." ON public.messages FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.role() = 'authenticated');
```

### Application Updates

1.  **Idempotent Table Handling**: The code now gracefully handles the existence of tables and ensures that `allUsers` (the Citizen directory) is kept in sync via real-time profile inserts.
2.  **Optimistic Syncing**: When you post or message, it updates locally first for speed, then broadcasts to the cloud.
3.  **Global Identity Persistence**: The `metadata` field in Supabase now securely stores your pet stats, streaks, and mood history so they follow you to any device.

